<section><div class="wrap">
  <div class="eyebrow reveal">Core runtime architecture</div>
  <h2 class="reveal d1">One control plane. One schema truth. Multiple transport surfaces.</h2>
  <div class="table reveal d2">
    <div class="tr"><div class="td">Rust control plane</div><div class="td">The whole system is a Rust control plane first: state, validation, bridges, and projections live in compiled Rust crates rather than ad hoc scripts.</div></div>
    <div class="tr"><div class="td">D-Bus projection</div><div class="td">Live authority is <span class="mono kv">org.opdbus.projection</span>; plugin objects publish under <span class="mono kv">/org/opdbus/v1/plugins/&lt;name&gt;</span>.</div></div>
    <div class="tr"><div class="td">PluginSchema</div><div class="td">Plugin is schema. If a validated schema/object is missing, the thing does not exist in the system.</div></div>
    <div class="tr"><div class="td">The Sled</div><div class="td">1:1 shared-memory layout for identity/state projection; schema-guided direct read/write semantics.</div></div>
    <div class="tr"><div class="td">The Shuttle</div><div class="td">Rust bridge/courier between D-Bus, gRPC, vector search, state projection, and UI surfaces.</div></div>
    <div class="tr"><div class="td">The Snowball</div><div class="td">Append-only session ledger and memory-loop substrate. Chat turns, tool actions, and approvals are appended here, then replayed into semantic search and UI evidence.</div></div>
    <div class="tr"><div class="td">Strike / Etch</div><div class="td">Hash generation and footprint binding for blocks, traces, and payloads.</div></div>
    <div class="tr"><div class="td">gRPC / UDS</div><div class="td">Internal service RPC over Unix sockets or controlled bridge paths; D-Bus remains authority, gRPC is transport.</div></div>
    <div class="tr"><div class="td">gRPC bridge</div><div class="td">Service-to-service APIs, event-chain search, assistant surfaces, and internal contracts flow over gRPC when they are not directly D-Bus-bound.</div></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section><div class="wrap">
  <div class="eyebrow reveal">Why these choices</div>
  <h2 class="reveal d1">Tonic, Gemma, and ZeroClaw each fill a specific role.</h2>
